Attribution

The core idea of a short list of "must-fix" generated-UI patterns (the "seven
cardinal sins") and the soft and polish tells that follow it are adapted and
condensed from the file docs/anti-ai-slop.md of the open-design project
(https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design), which is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. That file in turn credits the MIT-licensed refero_skill
(https://github.com/referodesign/refero_skill). The rule list in this repository
is a condensed and reworded adaptation. It was extended with detection logic,
severity levels, configuration, baselines, hooks and evaluation tooling that are
original to this project. The wording of the rules, documentation and linter
messages is original.

Files that contain adapted material
  skills/ui-anti-patterns/references/rules.md
  skills/ui-anti-patterns/SKILL.md
  skills/ui-anti-patterns/scripts/ui-slop-lint.mjs (rule selection)

Changes made to the adapted material
  Rewritten in new wording, merged with further rules, and turned into
  machine-checkable rules with tests.

